!Sample_source_name_ch1 = oligo array synthesis
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: cloned oligonucleotide library
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: 10-beta electrocompetent E. coli (C3020)
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = 2.4million cells were seeded in 10cm dishes. For plasmid-based MPRAs, the cells were transfected with 10 ug of plasmid libraries (HSS, ORI, and pGL4) using X-tremeGENE HP (Roche) with an Xtreme-GENE:DNA ratio of 2:1. For the lentiMPRAs, cels were infected with lentiviral libraries (5’/5’ WT/MT, 5’/3’ WT/MT, and 3’/3’ WT/MT) along with 8ug/ml polybrene, with the estimated MOI of 50 for wild-type and 100 for mutant libraries. Cells were incubated for 3 days. All experiments for nine libraries were carried out simultaneously to minimize batch effect. Three independent replicate cultures were transfected on different days.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Array-synthesized 230bp oligos (Agilent Technologies) were synthesized either containing the complete construct to be cloned or as overlapping fragments for Multiplex Pairwise Assembly or Hierarchical Multiplex Pairwise Assembly.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = other
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The cells were washed with PBS three times, and genomic DNA and total RNA was extracted using AllPrep DNA/RNA mini kit (Qiagen). Messenger RNA (mRNA) was purified from the total RNA using Oligotex mRNA mini kit (Qiagen) and treated with Turbo DNase to remove contaminating DNA.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For each RNA replicate, 3x500ng was reverse transcribed with Superscript IV (Invitrogen) using a primer downstream of the barcode, which contained a UMI. The resulting cDNA was pooled and split into 8 reactions, amplified with Kapa Robust polymerase for 3 cycles using an indexed P5 primer and P7. PCR products are then cleaned up with AMPure XP beads (Beckman Coulter) to remove the primers and concentrate the products. These products underwent a second round of amplification in 6 reactions per replicate and followed in real time with Sybr Green. All reactions were pooled at this point, cleaned up with AMPure CP beads, run on an agarose gel, and submitted for sequencing.
!Sample_description = Amplication from cloned library
!Sample_data_processing = Libraries were sequenced on MiSeq or NextSeq 500 instruments (Illumina) and base called using the instruments' Real Time Analysis software. Multiplexed paired end (PE) Illumina sequencing data was split based on sample index allowing up to zero substitutions in the barcode sequence. In some cases, technical replicates were concatenated to achieve sufficient read counts.
!Sample_data_processing = The MPRAflow pipeline (Gordon et al, 2019), freely available on Github, was used to process the MPRA data. A brief overview of this pipeline is described here:
!Sample_data_processing = For oligo validation, consensus sequences were aligned to all designed oligo sequences using BWA MEM (Li and Durbin 2009) with parameters penalizing soft-clipping of alignment ends (-L 80). For RNA/DNA counts, sequences were matched against the designed barcode sequences.
!Sample_data_processing = To normalize RNA and DNA for different sequencing depths in each sample, we divided reads by the sum of observed counts and reported them as counts per million. Only barcodes observed in RNA and DNA of the same sample were considered.
!Sample_data_processing = To determine the RNA/DNA ratios per insert, we summed up the counts of all barcodes contributing and determined the ratio of the average normalized counts.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh37
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: *elements.fa (FASTA) and *sequences_coordinates.tsv (tab-separated value) files contain all designed oligo sequences for barcode association mapping, along with chromosomal coordinates of each element, and element type (positive control, negative control, or other). *assignments.tsv.gz files contain the mappings between barcodes and their associated element, along with barcode counts supporting the association. *ActivityRatios*.tsv files contain RNA/DNA ratios for individual replicates or with replicates averaged.
